{"version":"1","id":"817bc9b5-113e-481c-9b35-2f1aa6b23576","handle":"phpdev","name":"PHP Dev","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--X4-DzKOE--/f_auto,q_auto/v1698161550/squads/817bc9b5-113e-481c-9b35-2f1aa6b23576","description":null,"is_squad":true,"x":-9.1405,"y":9.9813,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":19,"newest_post_at":"2026-05-01T08:45:44.575Z","oldest_post_at":"2024-06-24T07:48:47.676Z","features":{"hype_score":0.083333,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.111111,"avg_read_time":1.294118,"summary_length_avg":347.823529,"title_length_avg":50.888889,"title_length_var":285.209877,"tag_entropy":3.016298,"tag_diversity":1.789474,"top_tag_share":0.315789,"avg_upvotes":23.263158,"median_upvotes":4.0,"avg_comments":4.105263,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.17833,"zero_engagement_share":0.0,"viral_share":0.052632,"posts_per_week":0.196734,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"recency_skew":0.9},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.9412,9.5147],"cadence_depth":[-8.3676,-8.7353],"hype_variety":[9.2647,-1.8382],"title_style":[9.0,-1.1324]},"top_tags":[["php",17],["webdev",6],["laravel",5],["open-source",3],["devtools",3],["performance",3],["mysql",2],["wordpress",2]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["PHP 9.0 switch to BSD licence","DebugPHP is live. Free, open-source, real-time PHP debugging in the browser.","DebugPHP \u2014 Framework Support is here. Laravel logs, zero config."],"outlier":["I built a free MAMP PRO alternative with Rust \u2014 manage PHP, Nginx, MariaDB & SSL in one app"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"ZP5zzME3e","title":"PHP 9.0 switch to BSD licence","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/php-9-0-switch-to-bsd-licence-zp5zzme3e","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--qPvKM23u--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2009","num_upvotes":125,"num_comments":17,"created_at":"2026-05-01T08:45:44.575Z"},{"id":"cBHsNi8C1","title":null,"url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/cbhsni8c1","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--58gMhC4P--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2012","num_upvotes":30,"num_comments":14,"created_at":"2026-04-28T15:13:35.648Z"},{"id":"RdvLz6KGz","title":"DebugPHP \u2014 Docker support is here.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/debugphp-docker-support-is-here--rdvlz6kgz","summary":"DebugPHP Server now supports Docker with a three-command setup using Dockerfile and Compose config. Setting `dockerized: true` in the client config enables automatic server discovery by probing `debugphp-server`, `host.docker.internal`, and `127.0.0.1` in sequence, with results cached for an hour to eliminate per-request overhead. No hardcoded IPs or manual host configuration required.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--4oyMExWl--/f_auto/v1776762391/posts/DE7kOPiVO?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","num_upvotes":43,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2026-04-21T14:48:58.392Z"},{"id":"S76Kf58pD","title":"How can a property be not set and still exist?","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-can-a-property-be-not-set-and-still-exist--s76kf58pd","summary":"A PHP quirk where a class property can simultaneously appear unset, return true for empty(), and fail comparisons with falsy values. This edge case is described as an active bug affecting multiple developers, touching PHP's property initialization and type juggling behavior.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--xjA8IWkv--/f_auto/v1776283349/posts/S76Kf58pD?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-15T20:02:29.667Z"},{"id":"gpz8pvUrd","title":"DebugPHP \u2014 Framework Support is here. Laravel logs, zero config.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/debugphp-framework-support-is-here-laravel-logs-zero-config--gpz8pvurd","summary":"DebugPHP has added Laravel framework support, allowing developers to stream Laravel log output (Log::info, Log::warning, Log::error) directly to the DebugPHP dashboard with just two lines of code and zero configuration. No middleware, facades, or boilerplate required.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--yxzhqrfe--/f_auto/v1776259812/posts/2qf9RldSl?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","num_upvotes":50,"num_comments":6,"created_at":"2026-04-15T13:34:50.446Z"},{"id":"wYwXPeVAR","title":"EmDash aims to replace wordpress? Meh!","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/emdash-aims-to-replace-wordpress-meh--wywxpevar","summary":"A developer is building a PHP extension called 'king' that aims to bring async capabilities, QUIC support, service discovery, autoscaling, and an object store directly into PHP \u2014 eliminating the need for complex infrastructure stacks like Kubernetes or Docker. The project uses Cloudflare's Rust-based quiche library for QUIC integration and targets WordPress as the primary beneficiary, positioning it as capable of handling enterprise workloads, agentic workflows, video streaming, and real-time chat without additional languages or services.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--OSCRmANY--/f_auto/v1775782271/posts/W6UpwMf6X?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-10T05:00:13.039Z"},{"id":"F3LMdna1d","title":"DebugPHP is live. Free, open-source, real-time PHP debugging in the browser.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/debugphp-is-live-free-open-source-real-time-php-debugging-in-the-browser--f3lmdna1d","summary":"DebugPHP is a free, MIT-licensed, open-source PHP debugging tool that lets developers send any variable or data to a live browser dashboard using a single `Debug::send()` call. It requires no configuration, no desktop app, and no page reloads. Features include real-time log entries with filtering, table rendering, a built-in timer, live toolbar metrics, automatic environment detection, and click-to-open IDE integration (VS Code, Cursor, PhpStorm, Sublime). It has zero runtime dependencies beyond ext-curl, is fully self-hostable, and collects no telemetry.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--PDIIc-vF--/f_auto/v1775740904/posts/46tm9dT2V?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","num_upvotes":83,"num_comments":13,"created_at":"2026-04-09T13:22:33.007Z"},{"id":"ueHEiXXM9","title":"How to Improve Core Web Vitals on WordPress in 5 Steps","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-improve-core-web-vitals-on-wordpress-in-5-steps-ueheixxm9","summary":"A practical 5-step guide to improving Core Web Vitals on WordPress sites, covering server response times, caching, image optimization, JavaScript handling, and layout stability. Applicable to both blogs and WooCommerce stores.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--4VHFcF8A--/f_auto/v1774579924/posts/6Cqis23RW?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-27T05:38:55.465Z"},{"id":"35vP7OnAU","title":"I built a free MAMP PRO alternative with Rust \u2014 manage PHP, Nginx, MariaDB & SSL in one app","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-built-a-free-mamp-pro-alternative-with-rust-manage-php-nginx-mariadb-ssl-in-one-app-35vp7onau","summary":"LokcalDev is an open-source local development environment manager built with Tauri 2.0 and Rust as a free alternative to MAMP PRO. It provides multi-version PHP support (8.1-8.4), Nginx with site templates for WordPress and Laravel, MariaDB with phpMyAdmin, automatic SSL via mkcert, and local DNS management. The app is lightweight at ~15MB and available for macOS ARM64 and Windows x64.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--boU2yWtt--/f_auto/v1771222520/posts/ipuhrhcaa?_a=BAMAMiiu0","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-16T08:30:44.485Z"},{"id":"8PdYevAYD","title":"What if PHP could talk directly to the GPU?","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-if-php-could-talk-directly-to-the-gpu--8pdyevayd","summary":"A research project explores direct CUDA GPU access from PHP without Python intermediaries. The experimental PHP extension enables GPU tensor operations, operator overloading, async execution, and JIT-compiled CUDA kernels defined in PHP code. The project demonstrates GPU-accelerated array operations and custom kernel definitions using PHP attributes, pushing PHP beyond its traditional web development role into GPU computing territory.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--YE6iVXQG--/f_auto/v1769190841/posts/2oDuSvzKk?_a=BAMAMiiu0","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-23T18:17:00.108Z"}],"similar_handles":["dfa0u7-fs","allfrontend","c_community","webcraft","dotnetsquad"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","xai","hamelhusain","hwchase17","skirano"],"similar":[{"id":"DFA0U7-fS","handle":"dfa0u7-fs","name":"Pavan Belagatti","is_squad":false,"x":-9.1513,"y":10.072,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":11,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--r9dshbly--/f_auto/v1776930121/avatars/avatar_DFA0U7-fS?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":5.140243,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.181818,"avg_read_time":1.727273,"tag_diversity":1.454545},"top_tags_preview":[["ai-agents",8],["llm",6],["agentic-ai",4]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-0.4265,3.7794],"cadence_depth":[-9.6618,-8.0294],"hype_variety":[9.7941,-6.3971],"title_style":[8.5588,-5.7206]}},{"id":"5c31f101-d2eb-48fc-9b66-95a41066558f","handle":"allfrontend","name":"All Frontend","is_squad":true,"x":-8.938,"y":10.0046,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":14,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--6Jow1VVL--/f_auto/v1733384850/squads/5c31f101-d2eb-48fc-9b66-95a41066558f","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.239218,"median_upvotes":4.5,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.071429,"avg_read_time":1.357143,"tag_diversity":2.142857},"top_tags_preview":[["webdev",5],["nextjs",4],["react",4]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.3676,9.8382],"cadence_depth":[-9.0735,-8.6176],"hype_variety":[8.9853,0.5147